s9-3-p48 = prose (cons "Take a single \(C\) admissibly containing \(b_1{+\!+}b_2\) at \(a\). The **content** of the \(\mathsf{StablePrefix}\) and \(\mathsf{RelocOK}\) arguments in (9.13) includes proofs that this composite admissibility implies \(\mathsf{Admissible}(C,a,b_1)\) and \(\mathsf{Admissible}(C,a+|b_1|,b_2)\), respectively. Mere prefix/suffix containment is insufficient for an instruction whose decoding or branch behavior depends on its surroundings. These implications supply the *same* \(C\) to both block proofs. The first returns an intermediate state \(s_1\) at \(a+|b_1|\), and the second starts there; concatenate their execution derivations and trace lists. The composed trace contract is witnessed by \(s_1,t_1,t_2\). Placement or relocation must preserve branch destinations and the decoder equations; when the second block has already been certified at its final address, \(\mathsf{RelocOK}\) can be the identity placement witness, not a second relocation operation. These premises must be constructed, not inferred from concatenating bytes. For loops and continuing processes, the normal-exit block is replaced by a guarded step/trace correspondence." nil)
